# Show scripts

One file per show: `content-pipeline/scripts_input/<id>.json`. Shape is `ShowScript` in `packages/shared/src/script.ts`. Do not invent a different schema.

That file is the whole show: characters, locations (text only), prompt templates, and episodes. `content:frames` generates character stills from it, then each scene still from text.

- Character `promptBlock` is identity landmarks for the character still only. It is not pasted into scene stills or video.
- `locations.promptBlock` is the set, injected once. Do not rewrite the room in `imagePrompt`.
- `characterIds` is who fills the frame at the same size (at most two), not everyone in the scene.
- `imagePrompt` is camera, wardrobe, blocking. `videoPrompt` is motion and lines. The start PNG locks look for LTX — do not redescribe faces or the set there.
- Do not attach character portraits or location stills on a scene still.
- Every instruction the pipeline sends to Qwen or LTX comes from `prompts` (`characterImage`, `sceneStill`, `sceneVideo`) with `{placeholders}` filled from the matching fields. Do not hide prompts in Python.
- Valid show JSON only unless the human asked for a plan first.
